{
  "name" : "Leloup2003_CircClock_LD_REV-ERBalpha",
  "description" : "<notes xmlns=\"http://www.sbml.org/sbml/level2/version4\">      <body xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">        <p>This is model is according to the paper<i>Toward a detailed computational model for the mammalian circadian clock</i></p>        <p>In this model interlocked negative and positive regulation of Per,Cry,Bmal,REV-ERBalpha genes are all involved.The model is actually robust so the initial conditions are unimportant.We gave every entity zero as initial value,and start the graph at time=132h.</p>        <p>The simulation results in figure 8B can be reproduced by roadRunner online and Copasi. We use a ceiling function to simulate the day-light cycle.</p>        <p>This model originates from BioModels Database: A Database of Annotated Published Models. It is copyright (c) 2005-2011 The BioModels.net Team.<br />For more information see the <a href=\"http://www.ebi.ac.uk/biomodels/legal.html\" target=\"_blank\">terms of use</a>.<br />To cite BioModels Database, please use: <a href=\"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/20587024\" target=\"_blank\">Li C, Donizelli M, Rodriguez N, Dharuri H, Endler L, Chelliah V, Li L, He E, Henry A, Stefan MI, Snoep JL, Hucka M, Le Novère N, Laibe C (2010) BioModels Database: An enhanced, curated and annotated resource for published quantitative kinetic models. BMC Syst Biol., 4:92.</a></p>      </body>    </notes>",
  "format" : {
